WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.520
Donald Trump has been tweeting attacks on
protesters from the White House for days while

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:11.020
offering up a suggestion that the military
go in and use more force against protesters.

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:15.960
Meanwhile, Democratic presidential candidate
Joe Biden has been meeting with protesters.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:20.989
He gave a very good speech yesterday about
the state of the race as well as police relations

00:00:20.989 --> 00:00:22.199
in this country.

00:00:22.199 --> 00:00:27.029
And we now have Democratic Senator Elizabeth
Warren joining the protest marches yesterday,

00:00:27.029 --> 00:00:34.280
marching with her husband and her absolutely
delightful dog, a golden retriever named Bailey.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:38.530
Here is Warren marching, of course, with a
mask asked by a protester.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.440
Why is Donald Trump bringing in the military?

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.420
Warren says because he's wrong.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.620
People are protesting peacefully.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:46.620
Check it out.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.180
It is a little bit difficult to understand
all of the audio because people are wearing

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.901
masks, but I think you're going to get the
gist of it.

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:57.500
Why does it go wrong?

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:26.190
His wife says, yes, our people are test Elizabeth
Warren not being shy about what is going on.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:32.630
She tweeted on Monday, quote, The president
of the United States teargassed peaceful protesters

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:38.600
in order to clear the way for a useless photo
op outside the White House just after vowing

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:45.040
to activate the military against our own people,
lives and democracy are in danger.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.040
Danger.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.040
I like this.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.040
OK.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.040
She's a senator.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.810
She's not going to say everything you or I
would necessarily say, but she's being strong

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:52.810
and clear here.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:55.140
And how about Bailey, the dog at the protest?

00:01:55.140 --> 00:02:00.290
It really just doesn't get better than a nice
dog joining a movement for sanity and reason.

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:02.340
So what's going on with Warren as V.P.?

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:07.460
You all know, last week I interviewed Congressman
Roe Karna and he said he believes Warren is

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.649
the best choice for V.P.

00:02:09.649 --> 00:02:14.500
Joe Biden is increasingly getting pressure
not to pick Elizabeth Warren from different

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.560
camps.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:21.890
OK, there are some people who don't want Warren
to be the V.P. because they don't like her

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:26.030
wealth tax and they don't want her wealth
tax to be made into the law.

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:31.980
The reality is that Elizabeth Warren's wealth
tax is very unlikely to be made into the law,

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.980
even if Elizabeth Warren is vice president.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:35.500
Please understand that it's not even clear.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.220
Joe Biden supports that.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:42.370
There's another contingent that wants Joe
Biden to choose a black vice president.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:46.700
Now, remember, Joe Biden already committed
to choosing a female vice president.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:51.490
Yesterday on the bonus show, we talked about
the call for Joe Biden now to pick a black

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:53.540
female vice president.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:59.760
I believe that the top choices in terms of
who's likely to get it for a black female

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.990
V.P. would be Kamala Harris and maybe Val
Demings.

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:08.050
Now, Kamala Harris is hugely problematic because
of her actions as California attorney general.

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:14.650
Given what's going on right now with the protests,
it strikes me as maybe a bad idea to pick

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:19.210
Kamala Harris if in two months the protests
have died down, maybe it's something that

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:25.150
would be less problematic from a P.R. perspective,
although her track record as California A.G.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:26.569
is not good.

00:03:26.569 --> 00:03:29.970
Val Demings, on the other hand, would be an
interesting choice.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:33.300
She's a congresswoman from Florida with a
list.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:34.819
Florida, Georgia now.

00:03:34.819 --> 00:03:38.680
I believe it's Florida with a law enforcement
background.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:41.020
And I think that that would be a very interesting
pick.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:44.290
Now, there are people talking about Nina Turner
or Stacey Abrams.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.430
I know not everybody in my audience knows
who they are.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:54.030
I don't see it as even remotely likely that
Joe Biden picks Nina Turner or Stacey Abrams.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:55.490
So let me know your thoughts.

00:03:55.490 --> 00:04:04.000
Who do you think Biden is most likely to select
vs. who would you like Joe Biden to select?

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.069
Interested in hearing from you?

00:04:05.069 --> 00:04:06.819
You can let me know on Twitter at David Pakman

